diagnosis_text:
The user's report that PC0 (20.1.1.10) cannot reach PC12 (120.1.1.10) is not supported by any live evidence. A topology-wide reachability probe immediately after ticket intake showed 0% packet loss in both directions (pc0→pc12 and pc12→pc0, status "ok"). No "unplugged wire" exists: l2_snapshot confirmed all 15 devices have clean L2 identities with zero down or missing interfaces, and infra_sweep found zero ACL drop rules, zero static-ARP injections, and no gateway/resolver divergence on any host.

OSPF snapshot surfaced three flags (r8 orphaned area 0.0.0.2, r13 ospfd down, r12 no OSPF config), but direct config inspection explained each one. r12 and r13 both run EIGRP 100, not OSPF — ospfd absent on those devices is by design. r8 holds its stub loopback networks (18.0.0.0/8, 80.0.0.0/8) in area 0.0.0.2 where it acts as a single-router ABR; r8 itself has two Full OSPF adjacencies (to r5 via area 0.0.0.1, and to r4 via VLINK0) and is a healthy participant in the routing domain. The tc_snapshot and pressure_sweep were fully clean. No mechanism for a transient or historical loss event (flap script, carrier counter spike, syslog entry, stress tool) was found anywhere on the forwarding path. The network is operating normally; the maintenance report is incorrect.
